WEBVTT

00:01.175 --> 00:03.051
Travel to the ancient site
of Pompeii.

00:03.094 --> 00:06.430
I have hidden a key near
the cave canem mosaic.

00:07.223 --> 00:08.766
The key operates a vehicle

00:08.849 --> 00:13.349
that will allow you to safely
transport my daughter to me.

00:14.355 --> 00:17.066
Fugo! Abbacchio! Giorno!

00:17.233 --> 00:20.194
The three of you will travel
to Pompeii to get that key!

00:31.622 --> 00:36.122
<i>Heavy stones of fate
are holding down my dreams</i>

00:36.961 --> 00:40.464
<i>It feels as if I'm being crushed</i>

00:42.216 --> 00:46.716
<i>I've been staggering around
with nowhere to hide</i>

00:47.388 --> 00:51.225
<i>But I will never give in</i>

00:51.267 --> 00:55.767
<i>I know there are fragments of hope
buried beneath all that rubble</i>

01:03.070 --> 01:07.570
<i>I will find them with my own hands
and turn this world upside down</i>

01:16.125 --> 01:20.625
<i>Fighting gold
We will shine one day</i>

01:22.131 --> 01:26.631
<i>As long as we continue to
believe in our own path</i>

01:29.180 --> 01:32.349
<i>We are unyielding souls</i>

01:32.391 --> 01:36.891
<i>Our battle against god
will keep raging on</i>

01:37.647 --> 01:42.147
<i>Until our final days
Fighting gold</i>

01:52.036 --> 01:56.123
EPISODE 12
THE SECOND MISSION FROM THE BOSS

01:52.078 --> 01:56.144
Pompeii, ancient Roman resort
and city of culture and vitality.

01:56.999 --> 02:00.210
Then, in a fire storm of
volcanic ash and rock,

02:00.294 --> 02:04.172
the town was buried with
the eruption of Mount Vesuvius

02:04.340 --> 02:06.383
on August 24th, AD 79.

02:06.926 --> 02:08.510
Later, archaeologists' excavations

02:08.552 --> 02:09.803
revealed a metropolis
frozen in time,

02:09.845 --> 02:12.973
complete with villas, roads,
wine bottles, and carriage tracks,

02:13.099 --> 02:16.852
preserved just as they were
1,800 years ago.

02:17.186 --> 02:21.064
The cave canem is a mosaic
of a dog located in

02:21.148 --> 02:24.693
the vestibule of the so-called
House of the Tragic Poet.

02:30.616 --> 02:31.867
Oh, Fugo,

02:31.909 --> 02:34.369
we needed to turn right,
not left back there.

02:38.582 --> 02:41.251
Giorno, a little late now,
isn't it?

02:41.293 --> 02:43.128
Telling me we needed to turn right

02:43.212 --> 02:45.339
doesn't do me much good
at this point.

02:45.423 --> 02:47.258
You're absolutely right.

02:47.508 --> 02:49.510
Mi dispiace, I'll be sure to give
you some warning next time.

02:49.635 --> 02:53.889
This isn't about next time…
Huh, next time my freakin' ass!

02:54.557 --> 02:55.975
Hey, Fugo.

02:56.183 --> 02:58.268
We're kinda in a hurry.
Just cool it.

02:59.061 --> 03:00.353
You think I don't know that?!

03:04.400 --> 03:06.068
- Damn it…
<i>- It's annoying as shit,</i>

03:06.068 --> 03:07.652
- Damn it…
<i>- but this is typical Fugo.</i>

03:08.362 --> 03:12.862
<i>What's really getting under my skin
is this new guy, Giorno Giovanna.</i>

03:13.659 --> 03:16.078
<i>If Bucciarati insists we treat him
as one of our own,</i>

03:16.120 --> 03:17.538
<i>then I'll do what I have to do,</i>

03:17.580 --> 03:22.080
<i>but there's something
I just can't get past with him.</i>

03:23.085 --> 03:26.379
<i>Eventually, he's gonna
screw up big time…</i>

03:26.422 --> 03:28.632
<i>Whatever it is,
it could get us killed.</i>

03:32.386 --> 03:33.804
Pompeii, huh?

03:34.805 --> 03:35.806
Well, it's been a while.

03:35.890 --> 03:37.308
Haven't been there
since I was a kid.

03:40.019 --> 03:42.730
Abbacchio, Giorno, let's hustle.

03:49.570 --> 03:52.948
Our destination is now about
a hundred meters ahead.

03:53.991 --> 03:57.327
It should take us about
thirty minutes to get what we need

03:57.369 --> 03:59.412
and get back to camp.

04:05.753 --> 04:08.297
Abbacchio, Giorno, stay alert.

04:09.715 --> 04:11.758
Shit, well, that certainly
didn't take long…

04:12.051 --> 04:13.093
What's the count?

04:13.135 --> 04:15.554
I see one…
at least for the moment.

04:15.763 --> 04:16.972
He's creeping around,

04:17.014 --> 04:18.515
looking at us from
behind the pillar.

04:18.599 --> 04:21.643
The pillar…
Which one exactly would that be?

04:21.685 --> 04:23.520
Why don't you
open your eyes, Giorno?

04:23.646 --> 04:25.439
There's only one pillar.

04:25.481 --> 04:27.024
You can't see it
from over there?

04:27.191 --> 04:30.527
Fugo, you're definitely
right about that pillar,

04:30.653 --> 04:32.821
but I don't see
a freakin' soul either.

04:32.863 --> 04:35.574
I'm not messing around…
He's coming right for us!

04:38.702 --> 04:39.452
Fugo?

04:39.453 --> 04:41.329
That's him…
He's sauntering right over there!

04:44.458 --> 04:45.876
H-He was right there…

04:45.918 --> 04:48.420
A guy came out
from behind that pillar!

04:48.796 --> 04:51.089
I saw him in this mirror!

04:52.508 --> 04:55.010
W-What?!

04:55.052 --> 04:58.096
There! He's right there!
He's showing himself!

05:01.308 --> 05:04.644
H-He's inside the mirror?

05:07.398 --> 05:09.400
He's revealed his Stand!
Who's going to fight him?!

05:09.441 --> 05:13.528
Hold it, buddy… Nothing you've
said has made a lick of sense.

05:13.571 --> 05:15.239
Is something wrong
with the mirror?

05:15.447 --> 05:17.574
Merda…
He's coming in for the kill!

05:17.867 --> 05:20.536
Get away from the mirror!

05:22.663 --> 05:23.580
What?

05:23.622 --> 05:25.540
Giorno! Abbacchio!

05:28.961 --> 05:32.297
W-Where are you, Giorno? Abbacchio?

05:32.381 --> 05:33.548
Where did you go?!

05:35.634 --> 05:37.927
That freak in the mirror
has vanished, too.

05:37.970 --> 05:39.429
What did he do?

05:39.680 --> 05:41.932
Shit, the first red flag was
this creepy mirror

05:41.974 --> 05:44.142
hanging in the middle
of freaking Pompeii!

05:44.560 --> 05:47.563
Just what is it?
How does his Stand work?

05:48.230 --> 05:49.356
I don't…

05:50.190 --> 05:52.108
I don't know what it is…

05:52.610 --> 05:55.946
Something doesn't look right
about this place.

05:55.988 --> 05:56.989
I'm right here.

06:00.075 --> 06:01.701
<i>What?!</i>

06:04.455 --> 06:06.290
Pannacotta Fugo…

06:07.166 --> 06:10.335
You possess a high intelligence
with an IQ of 152,

06:10.419 --> 06:13.213
and entered university
at the age of thirteen.

06:13.255 --> 06:15.632
But a certain professor
rubbed you the wrong way,

06:15.925 --> 06:17.968
so you decided to beat him to
a bloody pulp

06:18.052 --> 06:19.887
with an anvil-like encyclopedia.

06:19.929 --> 06:22.806
The rest is, well,
a sad, sad and depressing history.

06:23.098 --> 06:25.433
You're accompanied by
the failed cop,

06:25.476 --> 06:28.020
Leone Abbacchio and…

06:28.687 --> 06:31.147
The data stops there…
He must be new.

06:31.523 --> 06:33.608
I think I heard
you call him Giorno.

06:33.651 --> 06:36.278
What did you do to them?

06:36.362 --> 06:38.197
Y-You bastard…

06:38.280 --> 06:41.324
Where did you hide them?!

06:46.121 --> 06:47.956
My watch is backwards?

06:48.123 --> 06:51.417
And now I'm wearing my watch
on my right hand?

06:52.544 --> 06:54.879
Miseria… This place is…

06:55.255 --> 06:56.881
So your Stand—

06:57.132 --> 06:59.968
Impressive,
so you really are a quick study.

07:00.010 --> 07:02.554
I like your eagerness, Fugo…

07:02.638 --> 07:04.890
But I didn't have
my heart set on you.

07:04.974 --> 07:08.560
You noticed the mirror first,
so you get to be number one.

07:08.727 --> 07:11.688
Abbacchio and Giorno
didn't disappear…

07:11.730 --> 07:14.190
This is some kind of
demented mirror world!

07:15.275 --> 07:16.484
I'm the victim here!

07:16.527 --> 07:19.363
That bastardo dragged me into
his own little playground!

07:20.739 --> 07:22.031
Fugo!

07:22.324 --> 07:23.908
Show yourself, Fugo!

07:23.993 --> 07:24.994
Hey, Giorno!

07:25.285 --> 07:27.120
Didn't you see anything?!

07:27.788 --> 07:29.164
I can't say for sure.

07:29.331 --> 07:31.708
One second I was looking at him,
the next he was gone.

07:32.501 --> 07:34.336
Fugo! Where are you?!

07:35.462 --> 07:36.880
<i>Right before he vanished,</i>

07:37.089 --> 07:39.382
<i>he warned us to getaway
from the mirror.</i>

07:39.425 --> 07:41.009
<i>And he asked whether we could see</i>

07:41.051 --> 07:42.719
<i>the man walking
from behind the pillar.</i>

07:43.387 --> 07:44.721
This mirror…

07:44.805 --> 07:49.305
Something is going on
with this mirror… What is it?

07:50.436 --> 07:52.187
The question is…

07:52.229 --> 07:55.565
Where did you hide
the boss's daughter?

07:55.607 --> 07:58.985
That, my amici, is of
the utmost importance…

07:59.069 --> 08:01.279
Then there's the question of
why you goons

08:01.363 --> 08:03.698
have come to the city of death.

08:03.824 --> 08:08.078
That is a piece of the puzzle
I cannot ignore.

08:08.370 --> 08:09.746
It doesn't take a genius to see

08:09.788 --> 08:11.915
you came here
searching for something…

08:11.957 --> 08:13.166
Which then would mean…

08:13.250 --> 08:17.045
you came here to collect a vital
something in protecting the girl.

08:17.087 --> 08:18.088
Correct?

08:18.213 --> 08:22.713
Just up ahead and around the corner
is the famous cave canem mosaic.

08:23.052 --> 08:25.054
Could that be where
I'll find the hidden prize?

08:25.095 --> 08:26.096
Well?

08:27.056 --> 08:28.766
Whatever it is, I'm taking it!

08:28.807 --> 08:31.768
Now make this easy and tell me
what this thing is, Fugo!

08:31.810 --> 08:32.644
Cazzi miei!

08:32.728 --> 08:34.354
So you choose death!

08:35.689 --> 08:36.773
Wrong, cazzo…

08:36.815 --> 08:40.193
The only one facing death will be
you when you gaze upon my Stand!

08:40.277 --> 08:42.112
Purple Smoke!

08:45.407 --> 08:47.617
What the hell is going on? I can't…

08:47.701 --> 08:52.201
I see… So Purple Smoke is
what you call your special ability.

08:54.958 --> 08:57.794
<i>Holy shit.
I know I roused my Stand</i>

08:57.836 --> 09:01.548
<i>I know it, I can feel it…
So why?</i>

09:03.425 --> 09:04.968
Hey, Giorno…

09:05.010 --> 09:07.137
I need you to walk
toward me, slowly.

09:08.722 --> 09:10.056
You need me to do what now?

09:10.099 --> 09:12.142
Just get your ass
over here pronto, fool!

09:12.267 --> 09:14.310
We're running out of time,
get the lead out!

09:17.147 --> 09:18.731
What?! Th-That's—

09:18.774 --> 09:20.650
Giorno! Forget about that!

09:20.859 --> 09:23.570
That's not the enemy…
It's Fugo's Stand!

09:24.321 --> 09:25.947
Quit dicking around and
get the hell away!

09:25.989 --> 09:27.323
It's suicidal…

09:28.117 --> 09:30.410
- Fugo's—
- Move away from Purple Smoke!

09:30.577 --> 09:32.245
Move quickly!

09:38.794 --> 09:41.671
I suppose I should be clear and
tell you are in a mirror.

09:41.713 --> 09:45.007
You, of all people, should know
why I pulled you in here

09:45.092 --> 09:47.260
all by your lonesome.

09:47.553 --> 09:51.223
Of course, bringing along
any of your fellow combatants

09:51.306 --> 09:54.600
could put in jeopardy
my own safety!

09:55.018 --> 09:56.853
I control all that
is within the mirror…

09:56.937 --> 09:58.647
That is my unique talent, you know?

09:58.772 --> 09:59.814
Everything you see before you

09:59.857 --> 10:02.609
is devoid of life,
completely inanimate.

10:02.651 --> 10:04.694
Only you and I have life
pulsing through our veins.

10:05.404 --> 10:07.906
I made sure to keep
everything else out.

10:07.990 --> 10:11.368
I permitted the entry
of you and only you.

10:11.535 --> 10:16.035
Catching on… Your Stand is waiting
patiently outside this place!

10:16.081 --> 10:19.084
Now get an eyeful of Mirror Man!

10:25.465 --> 10:28.634
<i>Purple Smoke materialized outside
the confines of the mirror.</i>

10:28.719 --> 10:32.389
<i>There's got to be
a way I can fightback!</i>

10:38.604 --> 10:40.564
MIRROR MAN
ILLUSO

10:41.523 --> 10:44.400
<i>Pannacotta Fugo was born into
a family of tremendous wealth,</i>

10:44.443 --> 10:47.487
<i>and lived on a vast estate
on the outskirts of Napoli</i>

10:48.155 --> 10:50.949
<i>He was blessed not only with
a life of luxury and privilege,</i>

10:51.200 --> 10:55.204
<i>he was also gifted with
a great intellect.</i>

10:55.245 --> 10:59.290
<i>To many, he lived
the perfect life.</i>

11:00.000 --> 11:04.500
<i>But the expectations placed on
young Fugo's shoulders were great,</i>

11:04.838 --> 11:09.092
<i>and his family and friends
were crushing him.</i>

11:12.304 --> 11:16.804
<i>At times, Fugo suffered bouts
of inexplicable rage,</i>

11:20.479 --> 11:23.815
<i>a kind of deep anger that
took all his might to contain.</i>

11:24.900 --> 11:28.987
<i>Then, as a university freshman
at just thirteen,</i>

11:29.071 --> 11:33.158
<i>his furor erupted into tragedy</i>

11:34.076 --> 11:35.452
Fugo.

11:36.203 --> 11:36.953
Professore.

11:36.995 --> 11:40.081
Now what could you be up to
at this ungodly hour?

11:40.666 --> 11:42.042
It's next week's assignment.

11:42.459 --> 11:44.461
I haven't found the appropriate
judicial precedent…

11:45.712 --> 11:47.338
Oh, don't be silly.

11:47.422 --> 11:49.841
You know that
you can always come to me

11:49.925 --> 11:52.302
with anything hard that arises.

11:52.469 --> 11:55.805
No, I wouldn't want to trouble you…

11:56.098 --> 11:59.226
Guiding and molding
bright young men like you

11:59.268 --> 12:01.436
is my scholarly duty.

12:01.853 --> 12:03.062
Come on…

12:03.105 --> 12:06.024
Come back to my house
for dinner and we can…

12:06.692 --> 12:07.567
Sorry, I have to go.

12:07.609 --> 12:09.277
Now, wait just a moment.

12:09.444 --> 12:10.987
I'd be more than happy
to share with you

12:11.029 --> 12:14.657
the questions that are going
to be on the next big test…

12:14.741 --> 12:18.369
- It'll be fine. Just relax, now.
- Stop… Stop…

12:18.453 --> 12:21.164
- Stop. Stop. Stop. Stop!
- I have a gentle touch…

12:21.248 --> 12:23.583
What don't you get about stop?!

12:26.003 --> 12:29.256
I looked up to you!

12:29.298 --> 12:32.050
You disgusting piece of shit!

12:33.719 --> 12:34.720
Did you hear?

12:34.803 --> 12:37.806
Supposedly, professore's been
getting real cozy with Fugo.

12:37.889 --> 12:40.057
You sure Fugo isn't the one
who baited the hook?

12:40.142 --> 12:42.519
That's probably how
he gets himself in this place.

12:45.272 --> 12:46.982
<i>Fugo's parents
leveraged their wealth</i>

12:47.024 --> 12:48.942
<i>to ensure all charges were dropped.</i>

12:50.152 --> 12:53.029
<i>But they no longer
treated him like a son.</i>

12:53.071 --> 12:54.906
<i>He was no longer a part of the family</i>

12:55.157 --> 12:56.575
<i>Without family or friends,</i>

12:56.658 --> 13:00.244
<i>Fugo turned to shoplifting and
pickpocketing for survival.</i>

13:00.579 --> 13:02.872
<i>Paradoxically,
it was his new way of life</i>

13:02.914 --> 13:06.626
<i>that would make full use
of his intellect.</i>

13:06.835 --> 13:09.587
Bastardo, think you can
just run away?!

13:09.671 --> 13:11.464
I'll make sure you rot in jail,
ragazzo!

13:11.506 --> 13:15.551
Sorry, but you, signore, will never
be able to put me behind bars.

13:15.594 --> 13:20.015
I assume you are not familiar with
De Sica vs. Argento, 1982?

13:20.432 --> 13:22.434
Considering the implications
of that case,

13:22.517 --> 13:24.602
it is highly likely that
the court will determine

13:24.686 --> 13:26.646
that I acted out of necessity.

13:28.440 --> 13:32.444
Signore Bucciarati, please
do something about this child!

13:33.862 --> 13:35.738
That's very interesting.

13:35.947 --> 13:39.075
<i>The visit coincided with
Bucciarati's own ponderings</i>

13:39.117 --> 13:41.744
<i>of forming his own team.</i>

13:42.579 --> 13:45.957
There, now you basically
know everything about me.

13:46.500 --> 13:48.668
You can stop feeling sorry
for me, okay?

13:48.835 --> 13:51.212
If it makes you feel any better,
I'm not unhappy.

13:51.254 --> 13:53.130
I see. But, well…

13:53.965 --> 13:56.425
I don't think it's chance
that you are here today.

13:57.094 --> 14:00.931
I'd like to invite you to
join my team, Pannacotta Fugo.

14:01.014 --> 14:03.307
Your intellect and knowledge
are one of a kind.

14:03.558 --> 14:06.102
Signore Bucciarati, correct?

14:06.561 --> 14:09.564
I've got nothing against
becoming a mafioso,

14:09.689 --> 14:11.273
but I've made up my mind.

14:11.483 --> 14:12.734
I'm done with people.

14:12.776 --> 14:14.319
I think it's best
I go it alone in life.

14:14.403 --> 14:15.862
Oh? And why is that?

14:16.071 --> 14:17.447
I told you.

14:17.531 --> 14:18.865
When I lose my temper,

14:18.990 --> 14:21.158
I become a monster
and do horrible things.

14:21.785 --> 14:25.789
If I joined your team, I couldn't
guarantee I wouldn't kill you.

14:26.123 --> 14:29.793
Well, I'm willing to put
that theory to the test.

14:29.960 --> 14:31.962
Leave your past and
come with me, Fugo.

14:32.045 --> 14:33.880
I promise you and your talents
will be respected,

14:34.005 --> 14:38.009
including your ferociousness and
your savage, impulsive nature.

14:39.886 --> 14:42.847
<i>His words stirred Fugo's soul.</i>

14:43.598 --> 14:46.642
<i>Soon, Fugo would
undergo Polpo's test</i>

14:46.685 --> 14:49.020
<i>and would acquire Purple Smoke.</i>

14:50.397 --> 14:52.190
So this is Fugo's Stand…

14:52.774 --> 14:54.317
<i>Fugo's no where to be seen,</i>

14:54.359 --> 14:56.611
<i>but somehow,
his Stand is right here.</i>

14:56.653 --> 14:58.404
He materialized his Stand.

14:58.447 --> 15:01.324
That means he's safe,
at least for now…

15:01.616 --> 15:03.993
Dammit, where the hell is he?

15:04.035 --> 15:05.703
How's he gonna protect himself?

15:08.915 --> 15:09.832
Get back, Giorno!

15:09.916 --> 15:11.709
That's not good enough.
Get the hell away!

15:12.419 --> 15:14.838
Fugo almost never manifests
his Stand.

15:14.963 --> 15:17.173
Only when
he's totally out of options.

15:17.257 --> 15:18.132
Which means,

15:18.175 --> 15:20.343
as you and I stand here right now,
Fugo is fighting for his life!

15:20.552 --> 15:21.886
Get further back, Giorno!

15:23.388 --> 15:25.223
<i>He seems more concerned
about that Stand</i>

15:25.307 --> 15:27.934
<i>than finding out
where Fugo has been taken.</i>

15:27.976 --> 15:29.852
<i>It's like he's threatened
or something.</i>

15:33.648 --> 15:35.983
What the—? Why would it be
lashing out all of a sudden now?!

15:36.026 --> 15:38.528
This isn't good.
We can't stay here a second longer.

15:38.612 --> 15:40.280
It's time to run! Come on!

15:40.322 --> 15:41.698
Nothing you're saying
is making any sense!

15:42.157 --> 15:43.867
Something is definitely lurking
in that mirror!

15:43.950 --> 15:45.368
It's critical that
we find Fugo now!

15:45.494 --> 15:47.537
Nothing else matters at this poi—

15:47.621 --> 15:50.457
I'm getting a little tired
of that mouth, pissant!

15:50.665 --> 15:53.334
I've never really given
two shits about you,

15:53.376 --> 15:54.543
but I felt sorry for you,

15:54.586 --> 15:55.920
so I thought I'd be nice
and give the newbie a heads up!

15:58.715 --> 16:01.259
It punched it! Run, Giorno!

16:03.512 --> 16:04.888
Interesting.

16:05.096 --> 16:08.057
So you activated your Stand
outside the mirror.

16:08.099 --> 16:10.810
But… that doesn't change a thing!

16:14.064 --> 16:17.317
It doesn't matter what kind
of tricks your Stand can do.

16:17.442 --> 16:20.278
Nothing it does can ever
have any affect on me.

16:20.362 --> 16:22.530
But I can make you my punching bag

16:22.572 --> 16:24.740
and finish you
whenever I feel like it!

16:27.869 --> 16:28.870
A crow?

16:29.371 --> 16:31.122
Why is a crow falling from the sky?

16:34.251 --> 16:36.294
A crow, without any warning…

16:36.378 --> 16:37.837
Stay back.

16:37.963 --> 16:40.006
When Purple Smoke uses its fists,

16:40.173 --> 16:42.633
you better hope
you're as far away as possible.

16:48.848 --> 16:51.559
What's with all
these dead animals?

16:54.771 --> 16:56.481
It's a lethal virus.

16:56.856 --> 17:00.109
That's Fugo's Stand,
Purple Smoke's ability.

17:00.193 --> 17:01.777
A virus?

17:01.987 --> 17:04.114
Look at those capsules
on his hand.

17:04.364 --> 17:07.700
When it strikes its fists against
something, the capsules shatter,

17:07.742 --> 17:11.120
spewing the infectious agent
contained inside into the air!

17:11.788 --> 17:14.707
Once airborne,
the virus infiltrates the body,

17:14.833 --> 17:17.085
either through respiration or
direct contact with the skin.

17:17.127 --> 17:19.254
It then multiplies violently.

17:19.296 --> 17:21.464
Viral pathogenesis takes place
in thirty seconds,

17:21.631 --> 17:22.798
after which death takes hold.

17:23.091 --> 17:25.218
And once the virus spreads,

17:25.552 --> 17:29.639
it doesn't matter who happens
to be nearby.

17:29.681 --> 17:30.932
Just like those crows,

17:31.057 --> 17:33.142
all metabolic functions
of your body will fail,

17:33.226 --> 17:36.145
and you'll die as you decompose
from the inside out.

17:36.271 --> 17:37.897
Of course, it'll destroy
your Stand too.

17:38.315 --> 17:40.317
What's its range?

17:40.483 --> 17:41.692
Five meters.

17:41.776 --> 17:44.278
The fact that
he can control his Stand

17:44.321 --> 17:46.239
means he's no farther
than five meters away.

17:46.615 --> 17:49.868
Okay, that's a good start,
but how far does the virus reach?

17:49.951 --> 17:53.454
I mean, at what distance is
the virus unable to infect a host?

17:53.496 --> 17:56.165
At this distance,
we should be safe.

17:56.249 --> 17:58.292
When the virus is exposed
to the elements,

17:58.335 --> 17:59.961
even a moderate amount
of indoor light

18:00.003 --> 18:02.296
can exterminate the virus
after several seconds of exposure.

18:02.797 --> 18:06.842
The sunlight should have
those crows disinfected soon.

18:07.594 --> 18:09.012
He's a beast!

18:09.304 --> 18:11.639
It blasts its victims with
a viral cloud of death,

18:11.806 --> 18:14.809
then melts away into nothingness
like a violent storm in the wind.

18:14.976 --> 18:18.688
What you're looking at is
the embodiment of Fugo's ferocity.

18:23.652 --> 18:25.111
What's it doing?

18:25.195 --> 18:28.198
Trying to wipe the drool off
his leg, I think.

18:28.239 --> 18:30.532
That deep, angry grimace
is like his signature.

18:30.617 --> 18:31.868
He's pretty neurotic.

18:32.202 --> 18:34.370
Seems even the slightest bit
of grime really irritates him.

18:34.454 --> 18:37.373
I guess every Stand's got
their own quirks.

18:52.472 --> 18:56.058
The Stand seems to be a bit lacking
in the intelligence department…

18:56.226 --> 18:59.729
We're seeing only the manifestation
of his savage side.

18:59.813 --> 19:04.313
It means Fugo can't
see Purple Smoke.

19:04.859 --> 19:07.236
He's having trouble
controlling him.

19:07.320 --> 19:10.156
He'd never let him act
like that otherwise.

19:11.825 --> 19:13.368
Its body…

19:13.410 --> 19:15.036
This crow is…

19:15.203 --> 19:17.788
It must be diseased or something…

19:17.872 --> 19:20.124
Like some bacterial or
viral sickness?

19:29.759 --> 19:32.970
I knew it… Fugo's lost
his grip on his Stand.

19:33.054 --> 19:34.180
He's doing it again…

19:34.222 --> 19:36.057
Another fit of rage
attacking things at random.

19:36.099 --> 19:38.851
<i>No, I don't think there's anything
random about this.</i>

19:39.227 --> 19:41.687
<i>There must be something
in that mirror!</i>

19:42.021 --> 19:44.815
Now he's gone and targeted
the mirror from the outside…

19:44.899 --> 19:46.734
You're wasting your time, Fugo.

19:46.901 --> 19:48.444
There's nothing special
about that mirror.

19:48.528 --> 19:49.862
You can find one like it anywhere.

19:49.904 --> 19:52.489
No matter what your Stand
tries to do out there…

19:52.574 --> 19:54.534
No matter what tricks
it has up its sleeve…

19:55.535 --> 20:00.035
Not even viruses can penetrate
Mirror Man's world!

20:01.082 --> 20:05.044
<i>Abbacchio, Giorno,
you have to understand…</i>

20:05.086 --> 20:08.047
<i>You can't let him drag you
into the mirror!</i>

20:09.424 --> 20:11.634
We need to hurry, Giorno!

20:15.263 --> 20:16.138
Hey, Giorno!

20:16.222 --> 20:18.307
Don't just stand there gawking,
move it!

20:18.349 --> 20:20.684
Help me understand…
Move it to where exactly?

20:20.769 --> 20:22.771
You don't mean to go find
the key, do you?

20:23.021 --> 20:24.647
You mean to tell me
you're considering ditching Fugo

20:24.689 --> 20:25.981
and letting him die?

20:30.945 --> 20:33.364
I strongly suggest you watch
your freakin' mouth, stronzo.

20:33.990 --> 20:37.076
Listen up.
Our mission is to get the key,

20:37.118 --> 20:40.371
and safely get that girl
to the boss!

20:40.538 --> 20:43.749
I want to save Fugo
as much as you do,

20:43.792 --> 20:46.961
but getting that damn key
outweighs all that!

20:47.462 --> 20:51.340
If I were the one trapped
inside the mirror right now,

20:51.382 --> 20:53.425
I'd want you to do
the exact same thing.

20:53.885 --> 20:55.678
I'm sorry,
but with all due respect…

20:56.596 --> 20:58.097
I think that's bullshit!

20:58.515 --> 21:00.350
Fugo may be in serious danger,

21:00.391 --> 21:02.643
but that doesn't mean
it's all over!

21:02.811 --> 21:05.313
We owe it to him to put it all
on the line to get him out of this!

21:05.355 --> 21:06.230
But before we do anything,

21:06.314 --> 21:08.524
we have to figure out how
this guy is attacking us,

21:08.608 --> 21:09.775
or we might as well hand
our lives over to him.

21:09.818 --> 21:11.444
Wrong. You think this is bad,

21:11.486 --> 21:14.197
wait until this bastard
takes all three of us out…

21:14.239 --> 21:16.658
I'll say it again!
It's time to carry on! Come on!

21:16.699 --> 21:17.866
And my answer's no!

21:17.992 --> 21:19.159
We'll unravel this mystery,

21:19.202 --> 21:20.953
rescue Fugo, and take down
this coward for good!

21:20.995 --> 21:23.247
That's the only way to
secure everyone's safety!

21:24.249 --> 21:25.375
Hate to break it to you, big shit,

21:25.416 --> 21:27.876
but I outrank you big time,
so what I say goes.

21:27.877 --> 21:29.587
Still have no for an answer?

21:34.509 --> 21:36.177
You'd better be prepared!

21:36.302 --> 21:39.513
That is, if you manage to survive!

21:44.811 --> 21:46.646
I'll ask you one more time, Fugo.

21:46.938 --> 21:49.440
What are you looking for here?

21:50.358 --> 21:52.693
Like I'd ever tell you, scum.

21:52.861 --> 21:53.903
I see.

21:54.070 --> 21:57.198
Very well.
There are still two others.

21:57.407 --> 22:00.868
I just need one fool
to tell me.

22:00.910 --> 22:03.662
It's time, my friend.
Now die!

23:38.257 --> 23:42.010
EPISODE 13
MIRROR MAN AND PURPLE SMOKE
